# Void Fluid Driller tooltip
vmd.mbtt.machine_type=Void Fluid Driller
vmd.mbtt.info.1=Extracts underground fluids without Mining Pipes or depleting chunk reserves.
vmd.mbtt.info.2=Use a Dimension Display block in the controller slot; leave empty for the current dimension.
vmd.mbtt.info.3=Input bus: programmed circuit config 1..N selects the Nth fluid in the dimension's list (see NEI).
vmd.mbtt.info.4=No circuit, config 0, or an out-of-range config prevents startup.
vmd.mbtt.info.5=Highest-tier drill head in the input bus: Iron x4, Steel x16, Titanium x64, Naquadah x256, Infinity x1024. 0.1% chance to consume one at cycle start.
vmd.mbtt.info.6=Per 100 ticks: 1000 mB x 4^(input tier - LV + 1) x 16^(machine rank) x 4^(drill class + 1). Iron is rank 0; no drill head means no boost. Infinity uses base 16 for the input tier term.
vmd.mbtt.info.7=Accepts LV+ energy hatches; uses the highest GT input tier.
vmd.mbtt.info.8=Draws 1 A at that input tier, independent of machine tier.
